   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 566 of the laws of 2019, authorizing the commissioner\nof general services to transfer and convey certain state land to the city of\nNew Rochelle, in relation to extending the authority of the commissioner of\ngeneral services to transfer and convey certain lands to the city of New\nRochelle",
    "basePrintNo": "S8266",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8266-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6, Chap 566 of 2019",
    "lawSection": "New Rochelle, City of",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8266\n\nSPONSOR: STEWART-COUSINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 566 of the laws of 2019, authorizing  the\ncommissioner  of  general  services  to  transfer and convey certain\nstate land to the city of New Rochelle, in relation to extending the\nauthority of the commissioner of general services to transfer and convey\ncertain lands to the city of New Rochelle\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the authority of the commissioner of general services to\ntransfer and convey certain lands to the city of New Rochelle\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends section 6 of chapter 566 of the laws of\n2019, as amended by section 1 of subpart C of part XX of chapter 55 of\nthe laws of 2020 to extend the authorization for the commissioner of\ngeneral services to transfer and convey certain state land to the city\nof New Rochelle until December 31, 2022.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2019, Chapter 566 was enacted to authorize the transfer of certain\nlands by the commissioner of general services to the city of New\nRochelle. That Chapter was subsequently amended by subpart C of part XX\nof Chapter 55 of the laws of 2020. The initial time period authorized\nfor the commissioner to transfer the land was two years from the date\nthe 2019 chapter was enacted, which was November 25, 2021. However, more\ntime is necessary to complete the transfer. This bill would extend the\nauthorization to December 31, 2022.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
